Material Properties for Metal
• In general, once AM processes are refined they can yield near wrought properties • Material properties are highly dependent on the type of process (L-PBF, DED, UAM, Coldspray,....), the starting feedstock chemistry, the parameters used in the process, and the heat treatment processes used post-build • Each AM process results in different grain structures, which ultimately have an effect on properties • Heat treatments should be developed based on the requirements and environment of the end component use • Properties should be developed after AM process is stable and parameters confirmed
